Three related deviations, all in how "which status is final" is decided.

**1. `list` hides `done`, contradicting its own POD and kanban-md.**
`Cmd/List.pm:159-161` filters on `is_terminal_status` (done + archived), while
the POD at `Cmd/List.pm:27` says "Archived tasks are excluded by default".

    karr list --compact  -> only #1 backlog     # #2 done is missing
    kanban list          -> shows #1 AND #2 done

kanban-md excludes only `archived` by default (`cmd/list.go:89`) and has an
`--archived` flag that karr does not implement.

**2. `is_terminal_status` is hardcoded** (`Config.pm:167-171`):

    return 1 if $status eq 'done' || $status eq 'archived';

On a board with columns `backlog, doing, shipped, archived`:

    karr move 1 shipped; karr pick --claim a
      -> "Picked task 1: t1 (claimed by a)"   # hands out a finished task
    karr list --compact -> "#1 shipped t1"     # and does not hide it either

kanban-md derives it from the config (`config.go:477`: the last status, or the
second-to-last when the last is `archived`).

**3. `handoff` hardcodes `'review'`** (`Cmd/Handoff.pm:59`) — on a board without
that column it writes an invalid status.

Fix: derive terminal status from the configured statuses, make the default
exclusion match kanban-md (archived only) and the POD, add `--archived`, and let
`handoff` take its target from the config.
Note from re-verification against main at 3dac607: `karr config set statuses ...`
answers "Key statuses is read-only", so custom statuses cannot be configured
through the CLI at all. They can still arrive through the config ref via
`karr import` of a kanban-md config.yml, which is the path that makes this
ticket bite. Whoever takes it should decide whether statuses stay CLI-read-only
(and this is purely an interop-robustness fix) or whether making the terminal
status configurable implies making the status list settable too.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 96 files / 654 tests.
Reproduced first, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix code.

#59: the predicate asked whether an attribute was SET, not whether it held
anything. Two further instances of the same root cause were found and fixed on
the way (list rendering an empty assignee, context reporting an empty due as
overdue); five more are split out as #98 with the one-line fix and the reason it
needs a deliberate decision.

#67 resolved as interop-robustness only: terminal status now follows kanban-md
(last configured status, or the one before it when the last is archived).
statuses stays CLI-read-only -- making the list settable means deciding what
happens to tasks parked in a dropped column, which is migration, not this
ticket. list still hides done AND archived by default (t/42 pins that as
intended); the missing --archived flag was added and the POD corrected.
